{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Apollonius_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Apollonius Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> interior to the region bounded by a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, such that the sum of squares of the distances from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the endpoints of a given diameter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/98444afa5befc74e29e616519b4112cbcdc15e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 0\\quad \\text{(B) } 1\\quad \\text{(C) } 2\\quad \\text{(D) } 4\\quad \\text{(E) } \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"272\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f1b0ab7f8460128d8a11d158014d0c95ee2480.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(circle((0,0),50)); draw((-50,0)--(-10,20)--(50,0)--(-50,0)); draw((-10,20)--(30,40)--(50,0),dotted); dot((-50,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(-50,0),W); dot((50,0)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(50,0),E); dot((-10,20)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,(-10,20),S); dot((30,40)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(30,40),NE);   [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"205\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be points on diameter.  Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and mark intersection with circle as point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341112a6db5e5d4daa8a2a367dbd6c774a3cc35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.  Also, by Exterior Angle Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a6571381f624606cd996806a1d89313d309c6445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB + \\angle CBP = \\angle APB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/4991ebc86e41e3cc4b9b8d0ce5d3c28b8a9ed298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB &gt; \\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dcab16d6a09e45436f7b9476391c37515455ee2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> an obtuse angle.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9bb0cd99c10ed989902fbcb86ac022df86ce3d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^2 + BP^2 - 2 \\cdot AP \\cdot BP \\cdot \\cos{\\angle APB} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"337\" height=\"16\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fa30345d49600aeba7ce8436f3159e12b1d363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^2 + BP^2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" />, substitute and simplify to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2ffa59ad1f27241d0aa1ff91bc52177337ed5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\angle APB} = -\\frac{1}{2 \\cdot AP \\cdot BP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"215\" height=\"37\" />.  This equation has infinite solutions because for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c553fd06c436a5133029fb384b8145adabbfd060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP + BP \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are both less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there can be an obtuse angle that satisfies the equation, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Apollonius_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Apollonius_Theorem)\">Solution 2 (Apollonius Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Apollonius Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be the circle with a centra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be any random point inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. Connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. \nWe want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fa30345d49600aeba7ce8436f3159e12b1d363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^2 + BP^2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" />\nIn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a87b39bd4072e5dc3edc67ee9ac5d8047c1ac4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APB, PO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> is a median on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Using Appolonius Theorem we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14bf942f3c3ff5ddb8eeec4624c55b46380bbdf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP^2 + BP^2 = 2(AO^2 + OP^2)\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9188447b4c80c3d56794ad70afca0d3999e829.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(OP^2 + 1) = 3\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690e03d0839b373e9e6be6c8502fc992b2dbd326.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\cdot OP^2 + 2 = 3\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/0373bbf9899deff83817b8667544de6fea824c69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OP = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>We draw a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> centred at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/9688e581d9cf8f2ac6b9d775b8e970f188e282f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> i.e, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\nEvery point on the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> will satisfy the given conditions. Since there are infinite points on a circle hence there are infinite number of points P that can satisfy the condition. \n</p><p>Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>--Tanstorm\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME\" title=\"1969 AHSME\">1969 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1969 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1969\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">31</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">32</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">33</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 34\">34</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">35</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017165943\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 349/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2746/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 176/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8535/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.327      1 -total\n 61.63%    9.446      1 Template:AHSME_35p_box\n 36.43%    5.583      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13070:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017165943 and revision id 258648. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}